  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 236 AM EDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\n- Areas of Frost this Morning, Sunday Night, Monday Night\n\nClear skies will aid in low temperatures dropping into the 30s \nbringing a risk for frost in inland areas mainly north of M-20. \nThere is also some patchy shallow fog developing toward the \nUS-127 corridor and along the lakeshore toward Ludington. Any \nshallow fog should quickly burn off within an hour of sunrise this\nmorning.\n\nFrost will be possible again Sunday night within a similar area to\ntoday. A risk for more widespread frost and potentially freezing \nconditions exists Monday night into Tuesday morning with lows in \nthe low to mid 30s.\n\n- Showers Sunday Morning then Mostly Dry\n\nA shortwave trough and associate front with swing through the area\nSunday morning with increasing moisture ahead of the front. Some\nscattered showers are possible largely north of I-96 with the \nbest chances (40 to 50 percent) north of M-20. With the recent\ntrends, would not be surprised if PoPs were increased over the\nnext few forecasts and extended further south.\n\nAs we head through the week west to northwest flow remains with\nsome embedded shortwave troughs. The question will be if moisture\nis present when these shortwaves move through. At this time with\nthe long range ensembles it is hit or miss with mostly dry\nconditions through the week. Overall not much confidence in rain\nany day beyond Sunday morning. Therefore will keep the NBM PoPs\nwhich show dry conditions.",
